From c7808ad9b6bee15d58943856df21b667ea85d677 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:11:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/59] ci: upstream's real-PBS e2e suite gates the release,
 both interop directions

- e2e.yml becomes a reusable workflow called by build-and-release.yml on
  every build; the release job needs it (it used to run on its own and
  gate nothing).
- New e2e test 9: an encrypted block backup made by the official
  proxmox-backup-client (compressed + encrypted chunks) is read back by
  our code through machinebackup/readback, a small helper reading a .fidx
  of the latest snapshot via pbscommon, and compared byte for byte.
- gofmt check extended to the files the fork adds or rewrites.
---
 .github/workflows/build-and-release.yml |  10 +-
 .github/workflows/e2e.yml               |  29 ++++--
 machinebackup/readback/main.go          | 119 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 testing/e2e/run.sh                      |  35 +++++++
 4 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 machinebackup/readback/main.go

